### The work-order state machine (`work_orders.stateMachine`), one job walked through every move.
###
###   new --schedule--> scheduled --start--> in_progress --complete--> completed
###   new | scheduled | in_progress --cancel--> cancelled
###   completed | cancelled --reopen--> scheduled                      (admin only)
###
### Each refusal is paired with the move that IS legal for the same caller on the same row, so a 403 is
### the transition's roles and not the row rule, and a 422 is the machine and not the field's shape.

### A job is created `new`. No `initial` binds creates (spec R1: imports arrive already scheduled), so
### this is convention rather than enforcement — the machine guards every MOVE.
# @name CreateNewJob
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-3101",
  "title": "Lifecycle: radiator leaking",
  "status": "new",
  "priority": 2,
  "access_code": "ACME-3101",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### `schedule` demands an assignee and a time (`when: has(new.assigned_to) && has(new.scheduled_for)`):
### without them the move is refused and nothing is stored
# @name ScheduleWithoutAssignee
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "scheduled" }

### The same move with both — the control that makes the 422 above the `when`, not the transition
# @name ScheduleProperly
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "scheduled", "assigned_to": "{{userTechNorth}}", "scheduled_for": "2026-12-01T09:00:00+00:00" }

### Skipping a step: no transition leads from `scheduled` to `completed`, whoever asks
# @name SkipToCompleted
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "completed", "completed_on": "2026-12-01" }

### The assigned technician may write the row (rules.update admits `assigned_to == @user.id`), but
### `cancel` lists only dispatcher and admin — the customer's job is not theirs to call off
# @name TechnicianCancels
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled" }

### The control: the SAME technician on the SAME row takes `start`, which lists technician
# @name TechnicianStarts
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }

### A PATCH that does not name `status` is no transition at all
# @name PatchNotNamingStatus
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Lifecycle: radiator leaking, valve replaced" }

### `complete` demands the sign-off day (`when: has(new.completed_on)`)
# @name CompleteWithoutDate
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "completed" }

### With it, the technician signs the job off
# @name CompleteWithDate
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "completed", "completed_on": "2026-12-01" }

### Only an administrator reopens a closed job: the dispatcher matches `reopen` but holds no admin role
# @name DispatcherReopens
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "scheduled" }

### The admin does
# @name AdminReopens
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "scheduled" }

### What the job ended as, read by the dispatcher
# @name ReadBack
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateNewJob.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
